course: dictionary
lesson: 6372
title: Muddy: more than mud
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Muddy» means covered in mud, or full of mud. It has comparison forms too: muddier and muddiest. You can also use it for things that are not clear, like cloudy water or a dull, mixed-up colour.
explain: Use the words around it to check the meaning. «Think of your bike in a muddy forest: sometimes walking is smarter.» A forest with mud everywhere makes riding hard, so muddy means soft, wet ground covered in mud.
explain: «Dolphins find food... sound travels well through water even where it is too muddy to see far.» The clue is «see far». If you cannot see far, the water is cloudy, not clear. Muddy can also be a verb: to muddy something is to make it muddy or unclear.
explain: Always test your meaning. Swap it into the sentence. If «muddy floor» means «floor covered in mud», the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: «Muddy» means covered in mud, or full of mud.
fact: Muddy water is cloudy, so you cannot see through it well.
fact: Wet, muddy paths and fields are slippery, so take care when you walk on them.
fact: «Muddy» can describe a dull colour, like the muddy brown you get from mixing too many paints.
fact: To «muddy the waters» means to make something confusing.
exercise: «His mum sees the muddy floor — āiyā!» What does muddy mean here? | Shining and clean | Full of music | Very cold | *Covered in mud
exercise: «Sound travels well through water even where it is too muddy to see far.» What does muddy water mean here? | Hot and bubbly | Crystal clear and sparkling | Frozen solid | *Cloudy, so you cannot see far
exercise: «Think of your bike in a muddy forest: sometimes walking is smarter.» Find and copy the word that describes the forest. | bike | walking | *muddy | smarter
test: Ella's boots are muddy after the football match. What does muddy mean? | Full of sunshine | Brand new | *Covered in mud | Very quiet
test: What does «muddy the waters» mean? | To go for a swim in the sea | To cook a thick soup | To clean a river | *To make things confusing
exam: Jayden writes, «The paint went muddy.» What does muddy mean? | The paint was sold in a shop | *The colours mixed into a dull, unclear shade | The paint was bright and shiny | The paint dried very fast
